assistant: Subject: convert cent prices from vendor 2026-10-01 to dollars
Starting with API version 2026-10-01, the vendor returns `price` in cents (119900) instead of dollars (1199), and the published spec wasn't updated to say so. `search_products` passed that number straight through, so agents were told prices 100 times too high. The handler in `src/tools/search_products.ts` now reads the `vendor-api-version` response header and divides prices by 100 when the version is 2026-10-01 or later. Responses from 2026-01-01 are left unchanged, so the v1 fixtures give the same output as before. The tool sends no new requests, and `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint` and `pnpm test` all pass, including the repro test. I didn't change `get_product`, which also passes `price` straight through, so it may have the same problem with the new vendor version.

